<main class="zd-founder-page">

  <section class="zd-founder-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-founder-eyebrow">Founder Journey</p>
      <h1>Building a better life, then building tools for others to do the same.</h1>
      <p>
        Ziyu Development is a founder-led project built around intentional technology,
        personal growth, learning, and the belief that software should help real life.
      </p>

      <div class="zd-founder-actions">
        <a href="/pages/projects" class="zd-founder-btn zd-founder-btn--primary">Explore Projects</a>
        <a href="/pages/support" class="zd-founder-btn zd-founder-btn--secondary">Support the Mission</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-founder-note">
      <span>Founder note</span>
      <p>
        This site is not just a store. It is the public record of building apps,
        products, and ideas that help people focus, grow, read, and live with intention.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-founder-story">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-founder-eyebrow">The story</p>
      <h2>Why I started building.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-founder-text">
      <p>
        I started Ziyu Development because I wanted to create technology that does
        the opposite of what most modern apps do. Instead of keeping people trapped
        on screens, I want to build tools that help people return to real life with
        more focus, purpose, and direction.
      </p>

      <p>
        The projects here come from real needs: building better habits, staying focused,
        reading better content, tracking personal growth, and creating a more intentional
        daily life.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-founder-timeline">
    <article>
      <span>01</span>
      <h3>Learning</h3>
      <p>Studying development, design, languages, business, and the systems behind better products.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>02</span>
      <h3>Building</h3>
      <p>Creating app ideas like Goal Grower, MyJourney, Blokkr, Kindlitt, and more.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>03</span>
      <h3>Documenting</h3>
      <p>Sharing progress through the journal, roadmap, build-in-public updates, and community.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>04</span>
      <h3>Growing</h3>
      <p>Turning the ecosystem into real apps, products, and tools that can help people.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-founder-values">
    <div class="zd-founder-section-head">
      <p class="zd-founder-eyebrow">What this is built on</p>
      <h2>The values behind the work.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-founder-value-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Intentionality</h3>
        <p>Every project should have a reason to exist.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Discipline</h3>
        <p>Real growth comes from consistent action over time.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Learning</h3>
        <p>Books, languages, study, and reflection shape the ecosystem.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Service</h3>
        <p>The goal is to build tools that actually help people improve their lives.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-founder-build">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-founder-eyebrow">Build in public</p>
      <h2>You can follow the process as it happens.</h2>
      <p>
        The roadmap, journal, and project pages show what is being built,
        what is still missing, what is improving, and what the long-term vision is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/pages/roadmap" class="zd-founder-btn zd-founder-btn--light">View the Roadmap</a>
  </section>

</main>

